Chapter: Microphone

 The Microphone effect is the right to listen to the machine's audio
 input. It is a bare marker here, the way Network and Display are: the
 operations that use it -- listen and is-quiet -- are not declared here.

 They were, once: two effect operations with no handler anywhere in the
 tree, so a call to is-quiet type-checked clean and then died at emit
 with CDX2040. Reading the microphone means driving the HDA input stream
 over MMIO, and that is codex.os, which a foreword chapter may not depend
 on -- so the honest place for them is not here. A chapter that wants
 them cites Kernel chapter MicInput and gets definitions that listen to
 the real audio codex-vm captures from the host microphone. A chapter
 that does not gets CDX3002 on the name -- the truth: it asked for
 something it did not bring.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Microphone where
